"""The agent slice: personas a person may chat with, their conversations and allowance, and an app-started job's watch.

A persona's chat is entered with its own `chat-<persona>` entitlement, known
only once the path is, so it is a dependency reading the path (`entered`),
marked as the module gate it is for the route walk. A conversation route
reaches the persona through the conversation: one answer for another
person's and for none, then the persona's own gate, so a revoked grant closes
a person's old conversations too. A shared answer is read through the
persona it was asked of, behind that persona's own gate, so whoever may not
chat with the persona is refused as they would be at its chat.

Which collections a person may read is the library's answer, asked as them
(`chat.collections`); this slice holds no list.

The job routes take `agent-<persona>` the same way, AND `CurrentWorkspace`:
a job belongs to a workspace and a persona, and `jobs.authorize()` checks
both (`app-factory docs/design/agent-jobs.md`). Starting a job is not a route; a person
watches, messages and stops one the app started.
"""

